WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.170
The newest Rogue One trailer included some moments that provoked major nerding out

00:00:04.170 --> 00:00:06.673
rom the Star Wars fans here in the Gamespot office. 

00:00:06.673 --> 00:00:11.219
Here are 3 potentially spoiler theories we came up with. 

00:00:14.681 --> 00:00:18.977
Jedha, the mecca of jedi religion definitely gets blown up.

00:00:18.977 --> 00:00:22.188
There is a line in the last trailer about a "new weapons test" being imminent

00:00:22.188 --> 00:00:25.400
and we think that Jedha is the target of that test. 

00:00:25.442 --> 00:00:28.153
Three of the Rogue One crew call Jedha home, 

00:00:28.153 --> 00:00:32.032
so that may be a major motivator to kick some imperial ass.

00:00:32.532 --> 00:00:35.577
We think the whole Rebel fleet is going to get some action. 

00:00:35.577 --> 00:00:40.874
The presence of Nebulon-B escort frigates, mon calamari cruisers, and corellian corvettes

00:00:40.874 --> 00:00:45.170
behind these x-wings are a good indication that the whole team came out to support. 

00:00:45.170 --> 00:00:49.215
This battle probably takes place in the orbital shipyards around the planet Scarif 

00:00:49.215 --> 00:00:51.634
where the Death Star was created. 

00:00:51.634 --> 00:00:57.640
 Just like in Return of the Jedi we may see a battle happening concurrently in space and on land. 

00:00:57.640 --> 00:01:03.063
 One on the surface of Scarif featuring cargo version of the AT-AT Walkers

00:01:03.063 --> 00:01:06.232
and one in space with the previously mentioned Rebel fleet. 

00:01:07.150 --> 00:01:10.570
Okay, it's going to get really theoretical in here for a second.

00:01:10.570 --> 00:01:14.908
I think Director Orson Krennic is going to redeem himself at the end,

00:01:14.908 --> 00:01:18.203
because Darth Vader looks so pissed off in this scene.

00:01:18.203 --> 00:01:21.831
 Based on an early synopsis from a book coming out in November, 

00:01:21.831 --> 00:01:27.337
Krennic was an old friend of Galen Ersa, the lead character's father.

00:01:27.337 --> 00:01:33.802
Maybe Vader is angry because he betray the Empire in the end to save his friends daughter.

00:01:33.802 --> 00:01:36.304
Or maybe he just messes up and gets force choked. 

00:01:36.304 --> 00:01:39.140
We nerded out really hard on a two minute trailer 

00:01:39.140 --> 00:01:40.140
so when the movie actually comes out we might explode

00:01:40.140 --> 00:01:47.065
For more on your favorite Comic books, TV shows and movies check out GameSpot Universe. 

